# ─── foundry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/lib/forge-std/.git

# contracts/broadcast is deliberately NOT ignored here. `forge init` writes a
# nested contracts/.gitignore containing `!/broadcast`, and a nested ignore file
# wins over a parent rule for paths inside it — so a `contracts/broadcast/` line
# here would silently do nothing and read as protection that isn't there.
# Foundry's convention is the right one anyway: real deployment logs are a public
# audit trail (they carry tx hashes, addresses and constructor args, never keys),
# while local anvil (31337) and dry-runs are excluded by the nested file.

# ─── the graph ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
